<title>USA: AFC Enterprises issues $175 million in 144A debt.</title>
<headline>AFC Enterprises issues $175 million in 144A debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144A debt issue from AFC Enterprises Inc was priced Friday via a Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co group, according to high-yield market sources.</p>
<p>BORROWER AFC ENTERPRISES INC</p>
<p>AMT $175 MLN	 COUPON 10.25 PCT  MATURITY 5/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 11/15/97 LAST MOODY'S B3    YIELD 10.25 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-B  SPREAD 357 BP     CALLABLE NON CALL FIVE</p>
<p>NOTE: Three year equity call for 40 percent at par plus coupon ((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
</text>
